# Files aider must not put in the repo map or let you /add. Same syntax as .gitignore.
# (Untracked/git-ignored directories such as node_modules, venv, models, jobs, output are already
#  skipped by aider because it only maps git-tracked files.)

# Huge or binary, no use to a language model
package-lock.json
public/fonts/

# ~10k tokens of canvas drawing code (one function). Larger than what the 16k-token editor model can
# take together with the rules, so editing it through aider produces garbage. To work on it anyway,
# delete this line and use --no-architect so the 24k-token model edits directly:
#   aider --no-architect public/js/05-avatar-draw.js
public/js/05-avatar-draw.js

# engine.py (~12k tokens) is NOT ignored — it is tracked and included in the repo map so aider
# knows what functions exist. But it is too large for architect mode. Always edit it with:
#   aider --no-architect engine.py
#   (or: tools/aider/task.sh engine tools/aider/prompts/engine-bugfix.md --no-architect)
# See tools/aider/ctx-engine.load for the full explanation.
